---
layout: empty
title: Book of Creation
description: "The Holy Book in-world of Stickverse. Based on Book of Genesis, it covers the initial creation of Stickverse itself, and The Creator's struggle against the Entropy system (known as the Deep) and the intricate balance The Creator must maintain to control the Deep."
draft: true
# The scribe's closing line, shown at the end of the book in Magika (Ancient Script) with the English beneath.
colophon: "[The scribe's closing line]"
# Translator's notes: how the Church's translation differs from this one. To attach a note to a verse, put
# {{ tn("its-id") }} right after the word it is about. Notes are numbered in the order they are listed here.
translatorNotes:
  - id: deep
    text: "[How the Church's translation differs here]"
---

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>{{ title or meta.title }}</title>

    {% include "meta.njk" %}
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link
        href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cardo:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=Cinzel:wght@400..900&display=swap"
        rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/main.scss">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/pages/creation.css">
</head>

<body>
    {# A translator's note marker; the note itself is in the front matter (translatorNotes) #}
    {% macro tn(id) %}{% for n in translatorNotes %}{% if n.id == id %}<sup class="creation-tn-ref"><a href="#tn-{{ id }}" id="tn-ref-{{ id }}" aria-label="Translator's note {{ loop.index }}">{{ loop.index }}</a></sup>{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endmacro %}
    <main class="container">
        <nav class="creation-return" aria-label="Back to fictions">
            <a href="/fiction/" class="cinzel-unique">← Return</a>
        </nav>
        <header>
            <h1 class="cinzel-unique">Book of Creation.</h1>
            <p class="creation-original ancient-script" aria-hidden="true">Book of Creation</p>
        </header>
        <section class="cardo-regular" id="chapter-1">
            <h1 class="cinzel-unique">Chapter 1</h1>
            <p>[1:1] In the beginning, The Creator exists. As the Creator exists, so does the everything and the deep{{ tn("deep") }}.
            </p>
            <p>[1:2] The deep was dark and filled with nothing, and the everything was shining yet malleable. </p>
            <p>[1:3] Then The Creator said, "<ruby class="creation-word"><span class="ancient-script" aria-hidden="true">Centro</span><rt>Centro</rt></ruby>"; and there was Centro. </p>
            <p>[1:4] The Creator saw that the Centro filled the nothingness with its shining light, and the universe is
                born.
                And The Creator saw that everything was eternal. </p>
            <p>[1:5] But then the deep came sweeping through everything, uninvited. </p>
            <p>[1:6] The deep must be satisfied, and The Creator tried to fill it with everything.</p>
            <p>[1:7] But the deep stood still, and instead covered the shining light, dimming it. And so the Day and
                Night was
                born. </p>
            <p>[1:8] As the Night passed, Day regained control, the first of its name has passed.</p>
            <p>[1:9] The Creator said, "<ruby class="creation-word"><span class="ancient-script" aria-hidden="true">Dome</span><rt>Dome</rt></ruby>"; and there was dome.</p>
            <p>[1:10] The Creator separated a part of the everything with the dome, in the center of the universe, and
                claimed it
                for Himself.</p>
            <p>[1:11] And The Creator said, "<ruby class="creation-word"><span class="ancient-script" aria-hidden="true">Earth</span><rt>Earth</rt></ruby>"; and there was earth.</p>
            <p>[1:12] The Creator formed a sphere of earth within the dome, and it fills itself with blue liquid. He
                calls it
                Land and Sea, and it was better.</p>
            <p>[1:13] And The Creator said, "<ruby class="creation-word"><span class="ancient-script" aria-hidden="true">Life</span><rt>Life</rt></ruby>"; and there was life.</p>
            <p>[1:14] The Creator infused the earth-sphere with life, and green colors of plants invade the land,
                seeding the
                first phase of Life into the sphere, and He was satisfied.</p>
            <p>[1:15] And the deep grew wary of the progress, and Night gains control.</p>
            <p>[1:16] As the Night passed, Day regained control, the second of its name has passed.</p>
            <p>[1:17] And The Creator said, "<ruby class="creation-word"><span class="ancient-script" aria-hidden="true">Stars</span><rt>Stars</rt></ruby>"; and there was stars.</p>
            <p>[1:18] The Creator create small shining lights that brights itself eternal, and it was so that they
                become the
                perceivable light for the earth-sphere.</p>
            <p>[1:19] And so the Night came, and the stars burned its light in defiance, one light burned brighter than
                the
                others.</p>
            <p>[1:20] And so Day regained control, the third of its name has passed.</p>
            <p>[1:21] And The Creator said, "<ruby class="creation-word"><span class="ancient-script" aria-hidden="true">Life</span><rt>Life</rt></ruby>"; and there was life again.</p>
            <p>[1:22] The Creator infused the earth-sphere with life, and things began forming in the sea, the first of
                the sea
                creatures was born.</p>
            <p>[1:23] The Creator waved his hand, and the sea creatures began multiplying itself. He was satisfied.</p>
            <p>[1:24] The deep grew even more wary, and quickly the Night gains control.</p>
            <p>[1:25] As the Night passes, the sea starts to fill with life quickly, and Day regains control, the fourth of
                its
                name has passed. </p>
            <p>[1:26] And The Creator passionately said, "<ruby class="creation-word"><span class="ancient-script" aria-hidden="true">Life</span><rt>Life</rt></ruby>!"; and for the third time there was life.</p>
            <p>[1:27] The Creator infused the earth-sphere with life, and things now form in the land. The first of the
                land
                creatures was born.</p>
            <p>[1:28] The Creator waved his hand, and the land creatures began multiplying itself. He was satisfied.</p>
            <p>[1:29] The deep now raged in its void, and as quick as He was satisfied, the Night gains control.</p>
            <p>[1:30] As the Night passed, the land began to fill with life quickly, and a surprise waiting to be seen. Day
                regains control, the fifth of its name has passed.</p>
            <p>[1:31] The Creator watched as the land creatures evolves, and some of them grew soft skin, light in weight, and
                it allows them to neither stay on land nor on sea.</p>
            <p>[1:32] The first of the air creatures were born, without The Creator's infusion of life. He was elated.</p>
            <p>[1:33] The Creator then said, "<ruby class="creation-word"><span class="ancient-script" aria-hidden="true">Stickmen</span><rt>Stickmen</rt></ruby>"; and there was Stickmen.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1 class="cinzel-unique" id="chapter-2">Chapter 2</h1>
            
        </section>
        {# The scribe's closing line: written in Magika, so it is shown in the script with the English beneath #}
        {% if colophon %}
        <footer class="creation-colophon">
            <p class="creation-colophon__original ancient-script" aria-hidden="true">{{ colophon }}</p>
            <p class="creation-colophon__translation cardo-regular">{{ colophon }}</p>
        </footer>
        {% endif %}

        {# The translator's notes: modern, so plain English only #}
        {% if translatorNotes.length %}
        <aside class="creation-notes" aria-labelledby="creation-notes-title">
            <h2 class="creation-notes__title cinzel-unique" id="creation-notes-title">Translator's Notes</h2>
            <ol>
                {% for n in translatorNotes %}
                <li id="tn-{{ n.id }}">{{ n.text }} <a href="#tn-ref-{{ n.id }}" class="creation-notes__back" aria-label="Back to the verse">↩</a></li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ol>
        </aside>
        {% endif %}
    </main>
    
    {% include "footer.njk" %}

</body>